134 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 73 0 R
/T (The single most transformative force in low-code development today is artificial intelligence. Platforms are increasingly allowing users to describe desired application functionality in natural language and receive working components, data models, or workflows in return. This goes beyond simple code-completion: emerging "agentic" capabilities allow AI systems to generate, test, and iteratively optimize application components based on observed usage patterns and predefined business rules, effectively acting as an autonomous collaborator within the development environment. Analysts project that a substantial share of all new application code generated through low-code interfaces will be AI-assisted or AI-generated within the next few years. )
/E (The single most transformative force in low-code development today is artificial intelligence. Platforms are increasingly allowing users to describe desired application functionality in natural language and receive working components, data models, or workflows in return. This goes beyond simple code-completion: emerging "agentic" capabilities allow AI systems to generate, test, and iteratively optimize application components based on observed usage patterns and predefined business rules, effectively acting as an autonomous collaborator within the development environment. Analysts project that a substantial share of all new application code generated through low-code interfaces will be AI-assisted or AI-generated within the next few years. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
