138 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 74 0 R
/T (Modern low-code platforms are increasingly designed around composability: modular, reusable components and services that can be assembled into applications much like building blocks. This trend aligns with the broader industry shift toward API-first and microservices-based architecture, allowing low-code applications to integrate cleanly with existing enterprise systems, third-party SaaS tools, and multi-cloud environments. Given that a large majority of enterprises now operate multi-cloud strategies, interoperability has become a key differentiator among competing platforms. )
/E (Modern low-code platforms are increasingly designed around composability: modular, reusable components and services that can be assembled into applications much like building blocks. This trend aligns with the broader industry shift toward API-first and microservices-based architecture, allowing low-code applications to integrate cleanly with existing enterprise systems, third-party SaaS tools, and multi-cloud environments. Given that a large majority of enterprises now operate multi-cloud strategies, interoperability has become a key differentiator among competing platforms. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
139 0 obj
<<
