/S /H2
/P 74 0 R
/T (4.2 Maturation of the Citizen Developer Movement )
/E (4.2 Maturation of the Citizen Developer Movement )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
140 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 74 0 R
/T (The citizen developer, a business user who builds applications without formal software engineering training, has moved from an experimental role to a mainstream contributor to enterprise application portfolios. With citizen developers now reported to outnumber professional developers by a wide margin at large organizations, enterprises are formalizing structured citizen-development programs that include training pathways, sanctioned tool lists, and review checkpoints, rather than allowing shadow IT to proliferate uncontrolled. )
/E (The citizen developer, a business user who builds applications without formal software engineering training, has moved from an experimental role to a mainstream contributor to enterprise application portfolios. With citizen developers now reported to outnumber professional developers by a wide margin at large organizations, enterprises are formalizing structured citizen-development programs that include training pathways, sanctioned tool lists, and review checkpoints, rather than allowing shadow IT to proliferate uncontrolled. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
