/T (As low-code applications move from departmental utilities to systems that touch sensitive data and critical business processes, governance has become a first-order concern rather than an afterthought. Organizations are introducing defined roles, mandatory approval workflows, and audit trails specifically for low-code artifacts. Centralized platform administration, environment segregation, and automated policy enforcement are increasingly treated as prerequisites for enterprise-wide rollout, particularly in regulated industries such as banking and healthcare. )
