<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 77 0 R
/T (Looking ahead, low-code development is expected to continue converging with artificial intelligence, moving toward increasingly autonomous, agent-assisted development workflows in which natural-language specifications are translated directly into deployable applications with minimal manual configuration. Governance tooling is expected to mature in parallel, addressing enterprise concerns around security and compliance that have historically limited low-code use for mission-critical systems. Analysts widely expect the proportion of new enterprise applications built using low-code or no-code approaches to continue rising, with AI-generated code accounting for a growing share of total application code produced industry-wide within the next several years. )
/E (Looking ahead, low-code development is expected to continue converging with artificial intelligence, moving toward increasingly autonomous, agent-assisted development workflows in which natural-language specifications are translated directly into deployable applications with minimal manual configuration. Governance tooling is expected to mature in parallel, addressing enterprise concerns around security and compliance that have historically limited low-code use for mission-critical systems. Analysts widely expect the proportion of new enterprise applications built using low-code or no-code approaches to continue rising, with AI-generated code accounting for a growing share of total application code produced industry-wide within the next several years. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [3]
>>
