/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 79 0 R
/E (New career paths are also emerging directly from this shift, including low-code platform administrators, citizen-development program managers, and hybrid engineers who specialize in extending low-code platforms with custom code and integrations where the platform's built-in capabilities fall short. For students specializing in fields such as Computer Science and Business Systems, which sit at the intersection of technical development and business process understanding, low-code platforms represent a particularly relevant area of study, since these platforms are explicitly designed to bridge technical implementation with business requirements. )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
224 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 79 0 R
/E (Compliance-driven industries have been particularly influential in shaping these governance capabilities. Financial services and healthcare organizations, both subject to strict regulatory obligations, have pushed vendors to provide detailed audit trails, role-based access control, and environment segregation between development, testing, and production stages. The net effect has been a maturing of low-code platforms from tools primarily focused on ease of use toward tools that also satisfy the compliance requirements of highly regulated sectors, which in turn has expanded the range of use cases considered safe for low-code implementation. )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
225 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 79 0 R
/E (Despite this progress, governance remains one of the most commonly cited barriers to low-code scaling. Enterprises frequently report difficulty tracking the full inventory of citizen-built applications across the organization, a phenomenon sometimes referred to as low-code sprawl. Addressing this typically requires a combination of technical controls, such as automated discovery and monitoring tools, and organizational measures, such as a designated center of excellence responsible for setting standards, providing training, and periodically reviewing the health of the low-code application portfolio. )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
