/Title (Education and retail sectors, while comparatively later adopters, are showing accelerating interest. Educational institutions are using low-code platforms to build student information portals and administrative workflow tools without dedicating scarce in-house engineering staff to routine administrative software. Retailers are applying low-code development to inventory management dashboards, loyalty program interfaces, and store-operations tools, often integrating these applications directly with existing point-of-sale and e-commerce systems through the API-first architectures discussed in Section 4.4. Across all sectors, the common driver remains the same: a persistent gap between the pace of business change and the capacity of traditional IT delivery to keep up.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 411 0 R
/Next 538 0 R
>>
endobj
