539 0 obj
<<
/Title (The single most transformative force in low-code development today is artificial intelligence. Platforms are increasingly allowing users to describe desired application functionality in natural language and receive working components, data models, or workflows in return. This goes beyond simple code-completion: emerging "agentic" capabilities allow AI systems to generate, test, and iteratively optimize application components based on observed usage patterns and predefined business rules, effectively acting as an autonomous collaborator within the development environment. Analysts project that a substantial share of all new application code generated through low-code interfaces will be AI-assisted or AI-generated within the next few years.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 532 0 R
>>
endobj
540 0 obj
<<
/Title (The citizen developer, a business user who builds applications without formal software engineering training, has moved from an experimental role to a mainstream contributor to enterprise application portfolios. With citizen developers now reported to outnumber professional developers by a wide margin at large organizations, enterprises are formalizing structured citizen-development programs that include training pathways, sanctioned tool lists, and review checkpoints, rather than allowing shadow IT to proliferate uncontrolled.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 533 0 R
>>
endobj
