546 0 obj
<<
/Title (procurement and custom development. Manufacturing and logistics sectors are applying low-code tooling to build internal operational dashboards and IoT-integrated monitoring applications.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 537 0 R
>>
endobj
547 0 obj
<<
/Title (Looking ahead, low-code development is expected to continue converging with artificial intelligence, moving toward increasingly autonomous, agent-assisted development workflows in which natural-language specifications are translated directly into deployable applications with minimal manual configuration. Governance tooling is expected to mature in parallel, addressing enterprise concerns around security and compliance that have historically limited low-code use for mission-critical systems. Analysts widely expect the proportion of new enterprise applications built using low-code or no-code approaches to continue rising, with AI-generated code accounting for a growing share of total application code produced industry-wide within the next several years.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 538 0 R
/Next 548 0 R
>>
endobj
548 0 obj
<<
/Title (At the same time, the role of the traditional software engineer is likely to evolve rather than disappear, shifting toward architecture, integration, governance, and the oversight of AI-assisted and citizen-built applications. Organizations that combine low-code adoption with strong governance frameworks and a clear division of)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 538 0 R
/Prev 547 0 R
>>
endobj
549 0 obj
<<
/Title (As low-code applications move from departmental utilities to systems that touch sensitive data and critical business processes, governance has become a first-order concern rather than an afterthought. Organizations are introducing defined roles, mandatory approval workflows, and audit trails specifically for low-code artifacts. Centralized platform administration, environment segregation, and automated policy enforcement are increasingly treated as prerequisites for enterprise-wide rollout, particularly in regulated industries such as banking and healthcare.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 541 0 R
>>
endobj
550 0 obj
<<
/Title (Modern low-code platforms are increasingly designed around composability: modular, reusable components and services that can be assembled into applications much like building blocks. This trend aligns with the broader industry shift toward API-first and microservices-based architecture, allowing low-code applications to integrate cleanly with existing enterprise systems, third-party SaaS tools, and multi-cloud environments. Given that a large majority of enterprises now operate multi-cloud strategies, interoperability has become a key differentiator among competing platforms.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 542 0 R
/Next 551 0 R
>>
endobj
